# ALERTS FEATURE — COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION DOCUMENTATION

**Project:** `car_sales`\
**Flutter package:** `car_sales_app` (folder `mobile_app`)\
**Feature root:** `lib/features/bottom/alerts/`\
**Framework:** Flutter and Dart (SDK `^3.12.2`, Flutter 3.44.8)\
**Platform:** Android\
**Market:** Ethiopia\
**Scope:** The Alerts tab (notification feed with read/unread states, swipe-to-dismiss, clear-all, and an empty "All Caught Up" state)\
**Purpose:** Act as the single source of truth for the Alerts feature. Inspect, repair, extend and verify the existing implementation without rebuilding working code.

---

# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

The Alerts feature provides a frontend-only notification feed for the car sales application. It must deliver:

1. A tab with title "Notifications" in the bottom navigation (index 4).
2. A header with the title and a "Clear all" text button (shown only when there are unread notifications).
3. A vertically scrollable list of notifications, each with read/unread styling, an optional car thumbnail on the right, an optional action button, and tap-to-open behaviour.
4. Swipe-to-dismiss on each notification (end-to-start).
5. A "All Caught Up" empty state shown when there are no notifications.
6. An automotive-themed illustration near the bottom of the empty state (bell + small car).
7. A `NotificationsStore` that handles marking read, dismissing individual items, and clearing all.
8. Mock notification data (`mock_notifications.dart`) that demonstrates all four notification types: `car`, `article`, `savedSearch`, and `general`.

## 1.1 Core rules

1. Inspect the existing project before editing anything.
2. Preserve correct and useful code. The notification row widget, swipe-to-dismiss, and empty state illustration are well designed and should be kept.
3. Repair broken code.
4. Update incomplete components.
5. Remove genuinely redundant code only after verifying it is safe to remove.
6. Reuse existing models, assets, navigation, state management and services.
7. Never duplicate the `AppNotification` model, the `NotificationsStore`, or the `mockNotifications` list.
8. Preserve New Cars, Used Cars, Compare and News functionality.
9. Use Ethiopian-market content and ETB prices where relevant.
10. Do not claim an integration works unless it has been verified on a device or emulator.
11. The Alerts feature is frontend-only. All data lives in `mock_notifications.dart`; when a real backend arrives, keep the `NotificationsStore` API (`items`, `unreadCount`, `markRead`, `dismiss`, `clearAll`) and swap the data source; the UI does not change (see the comment in `notifications_store.dart`).

# 2. FEATURE SCOPE AND NON-GOALS

## 2.1 In scope

- `AlertsScreen` (lib/features/bottom/alerts/alerts.dart).
- `NotificationsStore` (ChangeNotifier, singleton, lib/features/bottom/alerts/data/notifications_store.dart).
- `AppNotification` model (lib/features/bottom/alerts/models/app_notification.dart) with type, title, description, timeAgo, read flag, carImage, actionLabel, targetArticleId, targetCarName.
- `AppNotificationType` enum (car, article, savedSearch, general).
- `_NotificationRow` widget — single notification row with read/unread styling, optional car thumbnail, optional action button, and tap-to-open.
- `_EmptyState` widget — "All Caught Up" text + automotive illustration (`_AutomotiveEmptyIllustration`).
- `_AutomotiveEmptyIllustration` — circular card with bell icon + small car icon.
- Dismissible swipe-to-dismiss behaviour (Dismissible widget).
- "Clear all" button shown in the header when `hasNotifications` is true.
- `NotificationsStore.instance.unreadCount` for the bottom navigation badge.
- Named routes: `AppRoutes.alerts` (`/alerts`) → `AlertsScreen`; `AppRoutes.carDetails` → `CarDetailsScreen`; `AppRoutes.newsArticle` → `ArticleDetailScreen`; `AppRoutes.carSearch` → `CarSearchScreen`; `AppRoutes.placeholder` → `PlaceholderScreen`.

## 2.2 Out of scope (do not build in this feature)

- A real backend or API. All data lives in `mock_notifications.dart`; the comment in `notifications_store.dart` explicitly says "frontend only".
- Persisted notification preferences across app restarts. `NotificationsStore` is in-memory only (documented in section 22).
- Actual push notifications from a server. The feature is a local notification feed only.
- Deep linking to specific cars or articles beyond the hard-coded mock targets.
- A second notification store or duplicate data models.
- Video playback or live updates. The feature only shows static notification metadata.
- Indian rupee prices or lakh notation. All prices in the mock data are in ETB or N/A.
- Auto-mark-as-read on app foreground. The store only reacts to `markRead(id)` calls.

