## 3.1 Shared code rules

- `PageTopBar` is shared. Do not copy it.
- `AppIcons.news`, `AppIcons.notification` are the only icon needs (plus generic Material icons like `Icons.delete_outline` which are used directly).
- `NotificationsStore.instance` is the single source of truth for notification state. Both `AlertsScreen` and the bottom navigation badge read from it.
- All colour tokens come from `AppColors`. Do not hardcode hex values.
- All dimension tokens come from `AppDimens`. Do not use raw numbers.
- The `Dismissible` direction is always `endToStart`; the background is always a red container with a delete icon.

# 4. SCREEN FLOW AND NAVIGATION MAP

```
Bottom navigation (index 4, "Alerts")
        |
        v
AlertsScreen  (lib/features/bottom/alerts/alerts.dart)
  |
  |--- header: "Notifications" + "Clear all" (visible only when hasNotifications)
  |    |--- Clear all ---> clearAll() → pops all notifications + notifyListeners
  |
  |--- notification list (_buildNotificationList)
  |     |--- each row: _NotificationRow(notification)
  |     |--- swipe-to-dismiss (Dismissible end-to-start)
  |     |--- background: red container with Icons.delete_outline
  |     |--- onDismissed: store.dismiss(notification.id)
  |
  |--- tap a notification -----> _handleTap(context)
  |     |--- type switch: car → CarDetailsScreen(car) / not found → PlaceholderScreen
  |     |--- type: article → ArticleDetailScreen(article) / not found → PlaceholderScreen
  |     |--- type: savedSearch → CarSearchScreen() 
  |     |--- type: general → PlaceholderScreen(title: 'Notice', subtitle: 'More details coming soon.')
  |
  |--- "All Caught Up" empty state when store.items is empty
  |    |--- illustration: _AutomotiveEmptyIllustration (bell + small car)
  |    |--- text: "All Caught Up" + "You have seen all notifications"
  |
  |--- bottom navigation badge: Badge(isLabelVisible: unread > 0, label: Text('$unread'))
```

Rules:

- Swiping a notification left dismisses it from the store; the list rebuilds automatically via `ListenableBuilder(listenable: NotificationsStore.instance, ...)`.
- "Clear all" dismisses every notification and shows the empty state.
- Tapping a notification marks it read (`store.markRead(notification.id)`) and then navigates to the appropriate detail screen.
- Navigation targets are hard-coded per type; there is no generic "open URL" behaviour.
- The bottom navigation badge (`Badge` widget) shows the unread count; it is part of `BottomNavBar`, not the Alerts screen itself.

# 5. COMPLETE PAGE STRUCTURE

The Alerts tab is a single vertical scroll (ListView inside a ColoredBox) with these blocks in this exact order:

1. Header (`_buildHeader(store)`) — `PageTopBar` with title "Notifications", trailing "Clear all" button (conditional).
2. Notification list (`_buildNotificationList(store)`) — `ListView.separated` with `Dismissible` wrappers.
3. Empty state (`_EmptyState`) — shown when `store.hasNotifications` is false.

Do not split these blocks into separate screens. The page is one scrollable surface inside the bottom tab.

