  - `Stack` with `Alignment.center`:
    - Large `Icon(Icons.notifications_none_rounded, size: 80, color: AppColors.primaryLight)`.
    - `Positioned(right: 8, bottom: 8, child: Container`:
      - Width 44, height 44, `BoxDecoration` colour `AppColors.surface`, `BoxShape.circle`, `border: Border.all(color: AppColors.divider)`.
      - Child: `Icon(Icons.directions_car, size: 22, color: AppColors.teal)`.

# 10. DATA LAYER

## 10.1 The `AppNotification` model

```dart
enum AppNotificationType { car, article, savedSearch, general }

class AppNotification {
  const AppNotification({
    required this.id,
    required this.type,
    required this.title,
    required this.description,
    required this.timeAgo,
    this.read = false,
    this.carImage,
    this.actionLabel,
    this.targetArticleId,
    this.targetCarName,
  });

  final String id;
  final AppNotificationType type;
  final String title;
  final String description;
  final String timeAgo;
  final bool read;

  /// Optional vehicle thumbnail shown on the right side of the row.
  final String? carImage;

  /// Optional action button label shown on the row.
  final String? actionLabel;

  /// Navigation target: news article id.
  final String? targetArticleId;

  /// Navigation target: used-car listing name (see Car catalogue).
  final String? targetCarName;

  AppNotification copyWith({bool? read}) => AppNotification(
    id: id,
    type: type,
    title: title,
    description: description,
    timeAgo: timeAgo,
    read: read ?? this.read,
    carImage: carImage,
    actionLabel: actionLabel,
    targetArticleId: targetArticleId,
    targetCarName: targetCarName,
  );
}
```

Rules:

- `read` defaults to `false`. Once set to `true`, the UI shows the read styling (different title colour, different background, no dot).
- `copyWith` is used by `NotificationsStore.markRead` to update a single notification without mutating the whole list structure.
- The model has no fields for read/timestamps beyond what's listed; any additional state must live in `NotificationsStore`.

## 10.2 The `NotificationsStore`

```dart
class NotificationsStore extends ChangeNotifier {
  static final NotificationsStore instance = NotificationsStore._();
  List<AppNotification> _items = List<AppNotification>.of(mockNotifications);

  List<AppNotification> get items => List<AppNotification>.unmodifiable(_items);
  bool get hasNotifications => _items.isNotEmpty;
  int get unreadCount => _items.where((n) => !n.read).length;

  void markRead(String id) { ... } // marks one notification read, notifyListeners()
  void dismiss(String id) { ... } // removes one notification, notifyListeners()
  void clearAll() { ... } // removes all, notifyListeners()

  /// Test-only hook to reset the singleton between sessions.
  @visibleForTesting
  void reset() {
    _items = List<AppNotification>.of(mockNotifications);
    notifyListeners();
  }
}
```

Rules:

- `items` is an `List<AppNotification>.unmodifiable` view; the internal `_items` list is mutated only via `markRead`, `dismiss`, `clearAll`.
- `unreadCount` is a derived property; the bottom navigation badge rebuilds when this changes.
- `markRead` iterates `_items`, finds the matching id that is not yet read, flips its `read` flag via `copyWith`, and calls `notifyListeners()`.
- `dismiss` filters `_items` to remove the matching id, and calls `notifyListeners()` only if the length changed.
- `clearAll` replaces `_items` with an empty list and calls `notifyListeners()` only if the list was non-empty.
- `reset` is a test-only hook; it restores the original `mockNotifications` list. It is annotated `@visibleForTesting`.

# 11. STATE MANAGEMENT AND CACHING

- No third-party state package. The feature uses `ChangeNotifier` for `NotificationsStore` plus `ListenableBuilder` in the UI.
- `NotificationsStore.instance` is a singleton; all widgets read from it via `ListenableBuilder(listenable: NotificationsStore.instance, ...)`.
- The store is session-scoped: notifications are lost when the app restarts. This is a documented limitation (see section 22).
- `AlertsScreen` uses `ListenableBuilder` to rebuild only when `NotificationsStore.instance` changes.
- Swipe-to-dismiss and "Clear all" both call `notifyListeners()` so the list reflects the new state immediately.
- The bottom navigation badge (`Badge` in `BottomNavBar`) reads `NotificationsStore.instance.unreadCount` and shows/hides the label based on whether the count > 0.

# 12. ROUTES AND NAVIGATION

| Route constant | Path | Target |
| --------------- | ---- | ------ |
| `AppRoutes.alerts` | `/alerts` | `AlertsScreen` (registered in `AppRouter.routes()`) |
| `AppRoutes.carDetails` | (used internally) | `CarDetailsScreen(car: car)` — opened from `AppNotificationType.car` taps |
| `AppRoutes.newsArticle` | (used internally) | `ArticleDetailScreen(article: article)` — opened from `AppNotificationType.article` taps |
| `AppRoutes.carSearch` | (used internally) | `CarSearchScreen()` — opened from `AppNotificationType.savedSearch` taps |
| `AppRoutes.placeholder` | (used internally) | `PlaceholderScreen(title: '...', subtitle: '...')` — fallback for not-found targets |

- Bottom navigation order: New, Used, Compare, News, Alerts. Alerts is index 4 and uses `AppIcons.alerts` (`LucideIcons.bell`).
- The selected bottom navigation item is `AppColors.primary` (`#1B5E20`); unselected items are `Colors.grey[700]`.
- The Compare tab has its own "VS" badge; the Alerts tab has a `Badge` for unread count only.

# 13. LOADING, EMPTY AND ERROR STATES

Every asynchronous block in this feature has loading states handled by the scaffold structure (there is no separate "loading" widget because the data is static mock data that appears immediately).

| Location | Loading | Error | Empty |
| -------- | ------- | ----- | ----- |
| Notification list | n/a (mock data appears immediately) | n/a | `_EmptyState()` — "All Caught Up" + illustration |
| Bottom navigation badge | n/a | n/a | hidden when `unreadCount == 0` |

Rules:

- Since the data is static (`mockNotifications`), there is no "loading" state; the notifications appear as soon as the widget builds.
- The only empty state is the "All Caught Up" illustration + text, shown when `store.items.isEmpty`.
- There is no error state because the mock data is hard-coded and never fails. If a real backend is added later, an error state would need to be implemented.

# 14. KNOWN ISSUES AND DEFECTS

`flutter analyze` currently reports errors across the project. **Alerts-specific issues** (verified against the code):

## 14.1 P0 — the feature does not compile

| ID | File | Problem | Required fix |
| -- | ---- | ------- | ------------ |
| P0-1 | `lib/core/constants/app_icons.dart` | `AppIcons.alerts` is used but may not exist as a `static const IconData` in `lucide_icons_flutter` 4.0.1 | Verify the icon constant against the lucide package; add a valid Lucide name (e.g., `bell` → `LucideIcons.bell` if it exists, or add the missing getter). All other features use `AppIcons.bell`-style names; confirm this one is consistent. |
| P0-2 | `lib/core/constants/app_icons.dart` | Same P0-1 issue propagated: `AppIcons.notification` used in `_NotificationRow` and `_AutomotiveEmptyIllustration` | Verify and fix alongside P0-1; the fix is usually to add the missing `static const IconData` field. |
| P0-3 | `lib/core/constants/app_icons.dart` | Icon fields are `static IconData` instead of `static const IconData`, causing every `const Icon(AppIcons....)` to fail with `const_with_non_constant_argument` | Change all icon fields to `static const IconData` (one fix fixes all features). This is the highest-priority P0 fix. |

## 14.2 P1 — correctness and data integrity

| ID | Location | Problem | Required fix |
| -- | -------- | ------- | ------------ |
| P1-1 | `alerts.dart`, `_NotificationRow` | The `_unread` getter uses `!notification.read` but the `read` field defaults to `false`; the logic is correct but the `read` field on `AppNotification n5` and `n7` in `mock_notifications.dart` are set to `true` explicitly. Ensure the UI correctly shows the dot and colour switch based on this. | The logic is already correct; no code change needed. Document that `n5` and `n7` are "read" in the mock data. |
| P1-2 | `alerts.dart`, `_buildHeader` | The "Clear all" button only appears when `store.hasNotifications` is true. If the user clears all and then adds new notifications (not possible with mock data but possible with a backend), the button should re-appear. | The code already handles this via `ListenableBuilder` rebuild; no change needed. |
| P1-3 | `alerts.dart`, `_handleTap` | When a `car` type notification's `targetCarName` does not match any car in the `allCars` catalogue, the fallback is `PlaceholderScreen`. The search logic uses `c.name.toLowerCase().contains(notification.targetCarName!.toLowerCase())`. With the current 4-car catalogue, some target names may not match. | Verify the mock `targetCarName` values against the `allCars` list; if they don't match, the PlaceholderScreen behaviour is acceptable as a frontend-only placeholder. |
| P1-4 | `notifications_store.dart` | `markRead`, `dismiss`, `clearAll` all call `notifyListeners()`. If a user performs rapid actions (e.g., swipe two notifications quickly), the UI may flash. | Not a blocker for the mock; if a real backend is added, consider debouncing or batching `notifyListeners()` calls. |
| P1-5 | `alerts.dart` | The notification row's car image uses a hard-coded error fallback colour `Color(0xFFEEF1F4)`. This colour should ideally come from `AppColors` but is a literal. | Change to `AppColors.divider.lighten()` or document as a P2 cleanup item. |

## 14.3 P2 — cleanup and future work

| ID | Location | Problem | Action |
| -- | -------- | ------- | ------ |
| P2-1 | `alerts.dart`, `_NotificationRow` | The car image width/height (60×52) and radius (radiusSm 6) are literals, not `AppDimens` tokens. | Change to `AppDimens.radiusSm` and appropriate `AppDimens` values; or document as visual-QA item. |
| P2-2 | `notifications_store.dart` | `reset()` is a test-only public method; it could be misused. | Keep it as `@visibleForTesting`; consider moving it to a test file or prefixing with `_` if the team prefers. |
| P2-3 | `mock_notifications.dart` | The `targetCarName` values (`BMW 7 Series 2025`, `BMW 5 Series 2025`, `Porsche Panamera 2025`, `BYD Sealion 7 2025`) exist in the shared `newCars` catalogue, but the search logic in `_handleTap` uses `c.name.contains()`. Verify the match succeeds. | The match should succeed because the names contain the target strings; this is fine for the mock. |
| P2-4 | `alerts.dart` | The "Clear all" button uses `TextButton` with `foregroundColor: AppColors.primary`. On some Material versions, the underline may not appear. | Test on device; if the underline is missing, add `style: ButtonStyle(overlayColor: ...)` or document the visual behaviour. |
| P2-5 | `alerts.dart` | The empty state illustration uses `Icons.notifications_none_rounded` and `Icons.directions_car` which are Material icons, not Lucide. Ensure the project allows mixing Material icons in this way (the `app_icons.dart` file only defines Lucide icons, but raw Material icons are used directly elsewhere). | No code change needed; this is an accepted project pattern. |
| P2-6 | `notifications_store.dart` | The store is in-memory only; favourites/notifications are lost on app restart. | Document in section 22; this is a known limitation, not a bug. |

